---

Ramyan Reviews is a personal log of what I have been reading and watching — mostly novels, mostly slow films, and a steady diet of anime I have been meaning to revisit since university.

I am not a critic and this is not a publication. The ratings are a shorthand for how often I think about something afterwards, not a verdict on whether it is good. Five stars usually means it rearranged something; four means I would happily hand it to a friend.

Entries go up whenever I finish something and have more than a sentence to say about it. There is no schedule, no ranking, no year-end list.

> Kept like a reading log, not a scorecard.

If you want to argue with a rating, that is exactly the point of writing them down.
